WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:02.368
GRADY POWELL: Our undefeated
judge, Ben Abbott.

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:02.969
Ready to go.

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.671
[music playing]

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:07.240
[chopping sound]

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.375
Bring it on.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:12.678
The khanda.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:14.180
Hoo.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:16.315
NARRATOR: The khanda is a
sword that gained popularity

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:18.318
in medieval India
during the Gupta

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:21.554
period between 320 and 550 AD.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.723
The word khanda is
derived from the Sanskrit

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:28.394
word khan, meaning to break,
divide, cut, or destroy.

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:32.732
Its wide, thick, straight blade
was not only used for thrusting

00:00:32.798 --> 00:00:35.234
but also as a hacking weapon.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:38.070
When a Rajput warrior was
surrounded by the enemy,

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.339
he would pull out the
khanda and fight to the end

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.575
while swinging the
blade with both hands,

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:45.211
taking down as many
enemies as he could

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:49.148
in an honorable last stand.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:51.283
DOUG MARCAIDA: Bladesmiths,
this is a kill test.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.652
To test the lethality and
function of your weapon,

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:56.689
I will take your weapon and
deliver three vertical chops

00:00:56.755 --> 00:00:58.491
and then a slice.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.492
Ben, you're up.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.559
You ready?

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:01.994
Guess so.

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:04.596
[chopping sound]

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:07.667
[music playing]

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:13.573
DOUG MARCAIDA: Well,
Ben, the damage

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:18.077
that your blade did cut about 6
inches deep into both shoulders

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:20.313
and right through the spine.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.883
On the horizontal slice, pretty
much cut all the way through.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.552
It's got a good feel.

00:01:26.652 --> 00:01:29.054
This, sir, will kill.

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:30.890
- Thank you.
- Tom, it's your turn.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:31.891
You ready?

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.892
I'm ready.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:37.197
[chopping sound]

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:44.737
DOUG MARCAIDA: Tom,
you definitely cut

00:01:44.803 --> 00:01:49.842
in about 6 inches deep on the
shoulders and about 8 inches

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.143
into the spinal column.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:54.246
You cut halfway through
into the carcass.

00:01:54.346 --> 00:01:59.185
Also feels good in balance with
the downward vertical slice.

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:02.555
There was a slight bend that's
happening to your blade,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.191
but it will kill.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.563
Bladesmiths, this is
the sharpness test.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.865
I will slash across
these bungee cords.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:15.969
If your blade is sharp, it
should cut all the way through.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.804
If not, it may just push
it aside or bounce off.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:19.805
Ben, you're up.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:20.839
Are you ready?

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:21.974
Sure.

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.145
[music playing]

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.284
Shit.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:33.653
Well, Ben, your
sword started to cut.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:38.357
It cut a little bit, but
it did not cut through.

00:02:38.424 --> 00:02:42.027
It feels good on the slice.

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:44.330
The handle is very
comfortable in the hand.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.365
But once again, it
didn't cut through.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:50.269
So it brings into
question the sharpness.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.871
Tom, it's your turn.
Are you ready?

00:02:51.938 --> 00:02:53.038
I'm ready.

00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:54.706
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.277
[music playing]

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.378
Ooh.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.984
DOUG MARCAIDA: Well, Tom,
it did cut a little bit

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.385
into the bungee cord.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.855
But then as you see, that
transference of energy

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:10.056
went all the way
back to the blade.

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:12.024
It wasn't sharp
enough to cut through,

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.795
and it bent your
blade, which brings

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:18.897
to question the heat treatment
you did on your blade.

00:03:18.964 --> 00:03:20.499
Cut around corners, now.

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:22.668
It'll cut around
corners this time, right?

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:27.507
But this particular case,
it will not cut, sir.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.041
Gentlemen, both
of your weapons

00:03:29.107 --> 00:03:30.610
failed in the sharpness test.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.782
Historically, in
battle, blades bend.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.651
Tom, we'd like to give
you the opportunity

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.787
to straighten your
blade so that you

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:42.455
can continue with this fight.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:46.058
However, we will be taking
that bend into consideration

00:03:46.124 --> 00:03:47.593
when it comes to final judging.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.162
I understand.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:53.466
Should have left it thicker,
but I'm not a quitter.

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:55.601
I'm going to fight to the end.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.237
[hammering]

00:03:58.303 --> 00:04:00.540
OK, Tom, you've
straightened your blade.

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:03.542
We can continue with testing.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:04.743
Dave.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:07.446
DAVID BAKER: Gentlemen,
this is the strength test.

00:04:07.546 --> 00:04:11.150
I'm going to take five chops
into these copper pipes

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:13.953
and see how far
through we can split.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.787
Ben, are you ready?

00:04:15.854 --> 00:04:16.889
Not at all.

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.625
Yes.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:22.662
[pounding]

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:32.672
Wow.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:37.377
Ben, it's still one
piece, but barely.

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:43.049
And the dimensions of your guard
here on my hand are perfect.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.184
Your blade-- it's
held up beautifully.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.219
Nicely done.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:47.286
Thank you.

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:48.888
So Tom, your turn.

00:04:48.955 --> 00:04:49.855
OK.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.924
DAVID BAKER: All right.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:54.961
[pounding]

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:01.100
So Tom, what happened is we
lost a piece of the guard

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.668
right there.
- Yeah.

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:04.570
DAVID BAKER: With the broken
guard and the bend earlier,

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.873
I feel it's unsafe to continue.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.809
All right, thank you, Tom.

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:10.910
I'm disappointed.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.545
I know I could do better.

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:16.449
But that's what happens when
you don't use your time right.

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.921
Gentlemen, in just
five days, you've

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:25.424
both done an amazing amount
of work on your khandas.

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:28.227
But in this arena, there can
only be one "Forged in Fire"

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:29.462
champion.

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:38.671
Ben, you are the "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:05:38.771 --> 00:05:42.508
Tom, unfortunately, your
weapon did not make the cut.

00:05:42.574 --> 00:05:44.944
Please surrender your weapon.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:48.447
Well, I got to meet
some real nice craftsmen.

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:52.951
And I learned, don't let
your age slow you down.

00:05:53.051 --> 00:05:55.053
You don't know how long you got.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.422
Ben, congratulations.

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.324
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:01.260
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:02.295
Good job.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:03.662
Thank you.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:05.398
DAVID BAKER: Most people
get guard sizes all wrong,

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:08.601
and the khanda has a
deceptively small guard.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.135
You just hit it out of the park.

00:06:10.202 --> 00:06:11.570
Thank you.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.105
It feels amazing to be a
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:06:13.205 --> 00:06:16.776
It's a wonderful validation of
a long time of knife making.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.176
And I made new friends.

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.579
I made $10,000.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:21.914
What more could you ask for?

00:06:28.253 --> 00:06:30.089
HOST: The Scottish claymore.

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:31.023
Claymore.

00:06:31.123 --> 00:06:32.158
Yay.

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:33.425
Joy.

00:06:33.525 --> 00:06:34.927
NARRATOR: This massive,
two-handed sword

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:38.397
was wielded by Scottish
Highlanders as early as 1490.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.132
Made famous in
modern pop culture

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:43.502
by the film "Braveheart," its
impressive size and length

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.937
made it a fearsome weapon.

00:06:45.003 --> 00:06:48.407
The claymore is easily
recognizable by its quatrefoil

00:06:48.507 --> 00:06:50.443
crossguard and angled arms.

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:52.544
Due to its large size,
the heavy sword was

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:54.413
usually swung with two hands.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.448
It was so deadly,
it was nicknamed

00:06:56.515 --> 00:06:58.284
the slaughter sword
by the English who

00:06:58.384 --> 00:06:59.552
faced it on the battlefield.

00:06:59.618 --> 00:07:01.053
Because of its
prowess, the claymore

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:04.623
was a mainstay of the Scottish
army for nearly two centuries.

00:07:04.723 --> 00:07:06.525
WIL WILLIS: First up
is the strength test.

00:07:06.591 --> 00:07:08.995
As you can see, we've
brought back a test

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:11.396
worthy of a champion's blade--

00:07:11.496 --> 00:07:13.032
bullet splitting.

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:15.767
Each of your blades will
be locked into a vise that

00:07:15.867 --> 00:07:18.904
will fire a single round at
your blades to test their edge

00:07:19.004 --> 00:07:20.873
retention and strength.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.374
If your weapons are
strong, it should

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:24.310
split the bullet no problem.

00:07:24.376 --> 00:07:26.979
If they're not strong,
well, your blade

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:29.214
could shatter entirely.

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:30.182
Good luck.

00:07:30.282 --> 00:07:32.918
Matt, you're up first.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:34.753
MATT PARKINSON: I'm feeling
pretty good about my sword.

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:37.023
It's exactly the same heat
shield I did last time,

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:39.225
and it held up perfectly fine.

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:42.094
[music playing]

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:45.697
WIL WILLIS: 3, 2, 1.

00:07:45.764 --> 00:07:46.999
Engage.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:48.266
[gunshot]

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:49.235
[bleep] yeah.

00:07:49.301 --> 00:07:50.570
BEN ABBOTT: Nice.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.876
You got a couple of little
dimples on the edge, there.

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.744
It's just a little
bit dulled, but

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:00.412
everything held up beautifully.

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:01.380
Good job, Matt.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:02.414
MATT PARKINSON: Thank you.

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:03.482
Ben, you're up.

00:08:03.548 --> 00:08:05.150
Are you ready?
- Sure.

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:06.351
Let's do it.

00:08:06.451 --> 00:08:08.854
J. NIELSON: Let's get her ready.

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:11.056
3, 2, 1.

00:08:11.123 --> 00:08:12.725
Engage.

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.159
[gunshot]
BEN ABBOTT: Nice.

00:08:14.226 --> 00:08:15.194
MATT PARKINSON: There we go.

00:08:15.261 --> 00:08:16.862
[applause]

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:18.831
DAVID BAKER: Yeah that
sucker just fragmented.

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:34.847
Well, Ben, the only
problem I could see

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:37.382
is it rubbed a little
bit of your etch off.

00:08:37.482 --> 00:08:39.518
Did nothing at all to the blade.

00:08:39.618 --> 00:08:40.786
Edge is still perfect.

00:08:40.886 --> 00:08:42.020
Thank you.

00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:43.555
J. NIELSON: All right, next
up is a sharpness test.

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:45.991
And I'm going to hand you
over to Dave for that.

00:08:46.091 --> 00:08:48.460
Gentlemen, the Scottish
claymore, as you know,

00:08:48.527 --> 00:08:50.562
was a brutal weapon
on the battlefield.

00:08:50.662 --> 00:08:52.698
So to test the sharpness
of your blades,

00:08:52.764 --> 00:08:54.866
I'm going to take a
single blow through both

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:58.003
these front legs of the horse,
simulated with sugar cane.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:01.540
If your blades are sharp, they
should pass right through.

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:03.041
Matt, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:09:03.108 --> 00:09:04.043
Yeah.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.044
Kill the horse.

00:09:05.111 --> 00:09:07.813
[music playing]

00:09:16.422 --> 00:09:19.191
Matt, this weapon
is so amazingly light

00:09:19.291 --> 00:09:24.363
and flexible, as well, that when
I hit, there was no resistance.

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:26.299
It literally passed
right through the legs.

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:27.600
I was through them
before I knew it.

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:28.601
Well done, Matt.

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:30.603
Really well done.

00:09:30.703 --> 00:09:31.903
Ben, you ready?
- Let's do it.

00:09:32.003 --> 00:09:33.639
DAVID BAKER: All right,
let's give it a try.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.581
[cracking]

00:09:45.884 --> 00:09:47.018
MATT PARKINSON: He's still down.

00:09:47.085 --> 00:09:48.220
Yeah.

00:09:48.321 --> 00:09:50.790
Well, Ben, it cut cleanly
through the first leg.

00:09:50.856 --> 00:09:53.659
Kind of bogged down on the
second leg, unlike Matt's.

00:09:53.726 --> 00:09:56.395
And I have a feeling it's
the width of the profile

00:09:56.495 --> 00:10:00.632
up here just slowing
it down a bit.

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:03.168
But I don't think that
horse is running ever again.

00:10:03.268 --> 00:10:04.169
Nicely done, Ben.

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:05.571
Thank you.

00:10:05.638 --> 00:10:06.872
Next up is the kill test.

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:09.008
For that, I'm going to
hand you over to Doug.

00:10:09.074 --> 00:10:12.378
Bladesmiths, this
is the kill test.

00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:16.114
To see how lethal your blades
are, I will take your claymore,

00:10:16.181 --> 00:10:18.550
and I will try to cut
through these pig carcasses

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:19.952
with one chop.

00:10:20.018 --> 00:10:22.688
As you know last
season, both claymores

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:26.292
suffered catastrophic
failures on this very test.

00:10:26.358 --> 00:10:29.628
Let's see how much lethal
damage your blades can do.

00:10:29.694 --> 00:10:30.996
Matt, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:10:31.063 --> 00:10:31.864
Go for it.

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:33.099
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:10:42.675 --> 00:10:46.045
[slicing sound]

00:10:48.414 --> 00:10:49.348
It didn't break.

00:10:49.415 --> 00:10:52.585
That's the important part.

00:10:52.685 --> 00:10:55.821
DOUG MARCAIDA: Matt, I love
the feel of your blade.

00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:58.190
It feels very
comfortable in the hands.

00:10:58.257 --> 00:10:59.791
It's very easy to maneuver.

00:10:59.858 --> 00:11:03.762
It was sharp enough to cut
through in terms of lacerating,

00:11:03.863 --> 00:11:07.600
but it's just so flexible,
it didn't go through.

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:13.105
For this test, sir,
it will not kill.

00:11:13.205 --> 00:11:15.540
I'm pissed at
that pig right now.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:17.309
Ben, you're up next.
You ready?

00:11:17.376 --> 00:11:18.377
Hope so.

00:11:18.443 --> 00:11:19.412
DOUG MARCAIDA: Let's do this.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:30.890
[slicing sound]

00:11:33.959 --> 00:11:35.661
Ben, this blade
just sliced all

00:11:35.727 --> 00:11:37.963
the way through that carcass.

00:11:38.064 --> 00:11:39.564
It's flexible.

00:11:39.664 --> 00:11:42.301
It's got a good feel to the cut.

00:11:42.401 --> 00:11:45.003
This, sir, will kill.

00:11:45.070 --> 00:11:45.804
Thanks.

00:11:45.871 --> 00:11:47.639
MATT PARKINSON: Good job.

00:11:47.739 --> 00:11:48.941
All right, bladesmiths.

00:11:49.007 --> 00:11:50.943
You've given the judges
a lot to talk about.

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:53.412
We're going to have to go back
to the forge and deliberate.

00:11:53.512 --> 00:11:54.947
We'll see you there.

00:11:55.014 --> 00:11:57.583
Thank you.

00:11:57.649 --> 00:11:59.718
WIL WILLIS: Matt,
Ben, welcome back.

00:11:59.784 --> 00:12:01.687
The judges have
evaluated your weapon's

00:12:01.753 --> 00:12:03.656
performance and construction.

00:12:03.756 --> 00:12:06.258
Both of your weapons are
bulletproof, they're sharp,

00:12:06.325 --> 00:12:07.827
and they're deadly.

00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:10.196
But today, there can only be
one "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:12:17.269 --> 00:12:20.739
Ben, congratulations, you
are our first two-time

00:12:20.839 --> 00:12:22.441
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:12:22.508 --> 00:12:23.708
Great job.

00:12:23.775 --> 00:12:25.577
Matt, I have to ask
you to surrender

00:12:25.644 --> 00:12:27.346
your Scottish claymore.

00:12:27.413 --> 00:12:29.448
MATT PARKINSON: I'm a
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:12:29.514 --> 00:12:30.883
That's never going to go away.

00:12:30.949 --> 00:12:32.217
I don't feel like
I failed in this.

00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:34.186
I don't feel like I'm a
loser in this or anything.

00:12:34.286 --> 00:12:36.822
I just feel like Ben
did slightly better,

00:12:36.889 --> 00:12:39.425
and that's awesome.

00:12:39.492 --> 00:12:41.760
WIL WILLIS: Ben,
you are our first

00:12:41.827 --> 00:12:45.631
and only two-time "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:12:45.698 --> 00:12:47.966
You'll also be receiving
that check for $10,000.

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.402
DAVID BAKER: Your claymore
is a thing of beauty,

00:12:50.503 --> 00:12:53.672
not only to look
at, but to wield.

00:12:53.739 --> 00:12:55.341
- I'm at a loss for words.
- Thank you.

00:12:55.407 --> 00:12:56.274
DOUG MARCAIDA: Beautiful job.

00:12:56.374 --> 00:12:57.676
Oh, my god.

00:12:57.777 --> 00:13:00.445
I am the "Forged in Fire"
champion of champions.

00:13:00.512 --> 00:13:01.813
I can't believe it.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:03.983
The people I was competing
against are so good.

00:13:04.083 --> 00:13:06.484
To actually come out
and win this thing

00:13:06.551 --> 00:13:07.987
is absolutely amazing.

00:13:13.758 --> 00:13:14.994
HOST: The messer.

00:13:18.998 --> 00:13:22.000
The messer traces its origins
back to 15th century Germany.

00:13:22.067 --> 00:13:23.602
While these swords
range in size,

00:13:23.702 --> 00:13:26.705
they are distinguished by the
intricate hilts and guards.

00:13:26.772 --> 00:13:28.507
Back in season 6 of
"Forged in Fire,"

00:13:28.574 --> 00:13:31.009
two smiths were tasked to
recreate the massive version

00:13:31.076 --> 00:13:33.178
of this weapon, where the
competition ultimately

00:13:33.244 --> 00:13:37.182
went to the lighter,
better-balanced blade.

00:13:37.282 --> 00:13:41.119
DOUG MARCAIDA: Bladesmiths,
this is a dynamic kill test.

00:13:41.219 --> 00:13:43.823
To find out how lethal
your weapons are,

00:13:43.889 --> 00:13:46.057
I'm going to take your
swords, cut through the vines,

00:13:46.158 --> 00:13:49.895
and deliver some lethal
blows on this pig carcass.

00:13:49.995 --> 00:13:51.497
It's time to have fun.

00:13:54.733 --> 00:13:57.202
[music playing]

00:13:57.269 --> 00:14:00.239
[chopping sound]

00:14:14.353 --> 00:14:15.220
All right, guys.

00:14:15.287 --> 00:14:17.889
First up, the handle
construction--

00:14:17.956 --> 00:14:19.725
it's a little bit
on the blocky side.

00:14:19.825 --> 00:14:20.960
But it's comfortable.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:21.793
Why?

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:22.861
Because it's light.

00:14:22.928 --> 00:14:24.963
Every cut, every
one of them, was

00:14:25.029 --> 00:14:27.299
very deep on this pig carcass.

00:14:27.399 --> 00:14:30.769
Overall, this 8-hour
messer sword--

00:14:30.836 --> 00:14:32.071
it will kill.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:37.709
BEN ABBOTT: I'm pretty
confident that my sword

00:14:37.776 --> 00:14:38.777
is not going to break.

00:14:38.844 --> 00:14:40.312
But something might chip.

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:41.413
Something might roll.

00:14:41.513 --> 00:14:43.249
Anything is possible.

00:14:43.315 --> 00:14:47.252
I'm just nervous.

00:14:47.319 --> 00:14:51.891
[chopping sound]

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:18.350
So right off the bat, I
really appreciate the flare

00:15:18.417 --> 00:15:20.552
on a heavier blade
like this because it

00:15:20.652 --> 00:15:22.120
does allow me to control it.

00:15:22.187 --> 00:15:24.123
The weight of this
cuts very deep.

00:15:24.223 --> 00:15:26.892
It thrusts nicely and
delivers on the way out.

00:15:26.992 --> 00:15:29.494
A blade like this--

00:15:29.561 --> 00:15:30.596
it will kill.

00:15:33.432 --> 00:15:36.802
[music playing]

00:15:36.869 --> 00:15:38.537
All right, gentlemen,
a little bit of history.

00:15:38.604 --> 00:15:40.973
In 1570, Joachim
Meyer's treatise

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.742
on the use of the dussack
was published-- the training

00:15:43.842 --> 00:15:45.176
manual for the messer.

00:15:45.243 --> 00:15:47.045
So we know that
was used by peasant

00:15:47.111 --> 00:15:49.314
soldiers as well as nobility.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.718
So to that end, our
dynamic strength test.

00:15:52.785 --> 00:15:53.985
Gentlemen, I'll be
taking your messers

00:15:54.085 --> 00:15:56.020
and attacking our
armored warrior here.

00:15:56.087 --> 00:15:57.356
After that, we'll
see what kind of edge

00:15:57.422 --> 00:15:59.992
you have left by
slicing that painting.

00:16:00.058 --> 00:16:01.193
You guys ready?
- Oh, yeah.

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:01.994
Oh, yeah.

00:16:02.061 --> 00:16:03.228
DAVID BAKER: OK.

00:16:03.329 --> 00:16:06.632
[music playing]

00:16:09.601 --> 00:16:12.571
[metal striking]

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:28.954
All right, so right off,
it's taken a couple of rolls

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:31.223
that I can feel with
the fingernail and then

00:16:31.289 --> 00:16:33.291
a couple of small, minor chips.

00:16:33.391 --> 00:16:36.928
But for hitting armor,
it's not so bad.

00:16:37.028 --> 00:16:39.331
All in all, our gold
anvil did a good job.

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:46.071
[music playing]

00:16:50.776 --> 00:16:53.746
[metal striking]

00:17:09.327 --> 00:17:13.131
All right, so as far as the
edge goes, nothing's come off

00:17:13.198 --> 00:17:15.400
and nothing's
really rolled over.

00:17:15.466 --> 00:17:18.704
So all in all, I think the red
anvil did a really nice job.

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:26.044
GRADY POWELL: Now, guys,
the judges had a very

00:17:26.144 --> 00:17:27.312
difficult decision to make.

00:17:27.378 --> 00:17:29.247
And they came up
with a final decision

00:17:29.314 --> 00:17:30.949
that they both agreed upon.

00:17:31.016 --> 00:17:33.385
The winner of this "Forged
in Fire" competition

00:17:33.452 --> 00:17:40.458
is Ben Abbott with
the red anvil.

00:17:40.559 --> 00:17:41.626
Congratulations.

00:17:41.693 --> 00:17:43.228
No way.

00:17:43.295 --> 00:17:46.464
Now, Brandon, you absolutely
smoked this competition.

00:17:46.531 --> 00:17:48.967
But unfortunately, your messer
didn't make the cut today,

00:17:49.067 --> 00:17:51.336
and Dave Baker is
going to tell you why.

00:17:51.403 --> 00:17:53.871
Brandon, you did a
great job on that messer.

00:17:53.938 --> 00:17:55.673
It's fast, and it's deadly.

00:17:55.773 --> 00:17:59.877
This basically came down to
damage and some design choices.

00:17:59.944 --> 00:18:01.012
Fair enough.

00:18:01.079 --> 00:18:02.247
GRADY POWELL: I
can honestly say,

00:18:02.314 --> 00:18:03.248
you're one of the
most talented smiths

00:18:03.315 --> 00:18:04.516
I've ever laid my eyes on.

00:18:04.583 --> 00:18:05.684
Thank you.

00:18:05.784 --> 00:18:07.152
GRADY POWELL: We appreciate
all of your hard work

00:18:07.252 --> 00:18:08.386
in this competition,
but unfortunately,

00:18:08.453 --> 00:18:09.721
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:18:09.788 --> 00:18:10.989
step off the forge floor.

00:18:11.055 --> 00:18:12.490
- Thank you for the time, guys.
- Thank you.

00:18:12.591 --> 00:18:13.624
Good job, man.

00:18:13.725 --> 00:18:14.659
Awesome work.

00:18:14.759 --> 00:18:15.894
Thanks, Ben.

00:18:15.994 --> 00:18:17.395
Today just wasn't
my day, but I think

00:18:17.495 --> 00:18:19.531
I turned in an absolute
phenomenal blade

00:18:19.598 --> 00:18:22.701
that stacked up against one
of the best, Ben Abbott.

00:18:24.669 --> 00:18:26.204
GRADY POWELL: All right, Ben.
You did it.

00:18:26.271 --> 00:18:27.939
Your messer took
home the win, again.

00:18:28.006 --> 00:18:28.940
You're now 5 and 0, man.

00:18:29.007 --> 00:18:31.409
Congratulations.

00:18:31.476 --> 00:18:33.378
BEN ABBOTT: This was an
extremely close competition.

00:18:33.445 --> 00:18:35.313
Brandon is a hell
of a competitor.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:36.882
He made a really
good messer sword.

00:18:36.982 --> 00:18:42.053
And I was actually practicing my
happy-faced concession speech.

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:43.788
You ready for more?

00:18:43.855 --> 00:18:45.290
Yep.
Let's do it.

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:46.892
Any bladesmiths who
want to come in here

00:18:46.992 --> 00:18:51.263
and challenge me in my own
house, I'm here, ready for you.

00:18:54.265 --> 00:18:57.269
GRADY POWELL: The Irish,
ring-hilted sword.

00:18:57.336 --> 00:18:58.837
Oh.

00:18:58.904 --> 00:19:00.205
NARRATOR: The Irish
ring sword was

00:19:00.305 --> 00:19:01.973
a weapon of the elite,
Gallowglass mercenaries

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:03.575
in 12th century Ireland.

00:19:03.642 --> 00:19:05.477
This extremely long,
double-edged sword

00:19:05.544 --> 00:19:07.779
was featured in season 5
of "Forged in Fire," where

00:19:07.845 --> 00:19:10.849
the Smiths were challenged with
not only having to forge out

00:19:10.916 --> 00:19:13.718
something of this length,
but also the added challenge

00:19:13.785 --> 00:19:15.187
of putting a fuller in it.

00:19:15.254 --> 00:19:17.689
While both smiths struggled
to make such a long blade

00:19:17.789 --> 00:19:21.559
both light and strong, one smith
went too thin in his design,

00:19:21.659 --> 00:19:26.031
causing a bend in testing and
costing him the competition.

00:19:26.131 --> 00:19:27.299
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, bladesmiths.

00:19:27.366 --> 00:19:30.335
Welcome to the
dynamic kill test.

00:19:30.435 --> 00:19:31.937
To find out how lethal
your weapons are,

00:19:32.037 --> 00:19:34.339
I'm going to deliver some deadly
blows on this ballistics dummy

00:19:34.406 --> 00:19:35.841
and cut some water tubes.

00:19:40.078 --> 00:19:42.980
[music playing]

00:19:43.081 --> 00:19:46.652
[chopping sound]

00:20:06.305 --> 00:20:07.405
All right, guys.

00:20:07.505 --> 00:20:09.540
When delivering
the cuts over here,

00:20:09.607 --> 00:20:12.276
they slash nicely
through the water tubes

00:20:12.343 --> 00:20:14.646
and just demolish
that ballistics dummy.

00:20:14.746 --> 00:20:17.315
On that piece, probably
ran out of blade

00:20:17.381 --> 00:20:18.850
as I'm cutting on the backhand.

00:20:18.951 --> 00:20:22.320
But as you can see, the
cuts, they are very sharp.

00:20:22.386 --> 00:20:26.491
Overall, it will kill and cut.

00:20:26.558 --> 00:20:29.494
I'd say so.

00:20:29.595 --> 00:20:33.232
[music playing]

00:20:35.601 --> 00:20:38.971
[chopping sound]

00:20:59.924 --> 00:21:02.794
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right,
first up, when I pick this up,

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.863
you can tell there's a big
difference in the weight.

00:21:05.963 --> 00:21:07.231
The edge is sharp.

00:21:07.332 --> 00:21:10.368
So when I'm chopping into
the ballistics dummy,

00:21:10.468 --> 00:21:15.307
it's a deep cut, but it's
heavier and harder to control.

00:21:15.374 --> 00:21:18.543
It cut the first two tubes,
and then pushed the rest.

00:21:18.643 --> 00:21:21.212
But overall, looking at the
damage to the ballistics dummy

00:21:21.312 --> 00:21:24.283
and some of the
cuts, it will kill.

00:21:28.286 --> 00:21:29.454
DAVID BAKER: All
right, gentlemen,

00:21:29.554 --> 00:21:30.822
it's time for our
dynamic strength test--

00:21:30.889 --> 00:21:34.159
the bamboo sword chop
and tatami mat slice.

00:21:34.226 --> 00:21:36.028
I'm not only looking at
how well your weapons

00:21:36.128 --> 00:21:37.995
hold up in this test
but how they feel

00:21:38.062 --> 00:21:39.431
and how well they cut.

00:21:39.498 --> 00:21:40.766
Silver is up first.

00:21:44.936 --> 00:21:48.807
[music playing]

00:21:48.874 --> 00:21:51.843
[striking sound]

00:22:05.524 --> 00:22:08.326
All right, guys, right off, the
blade is really, really light.

00:22:08.426 --> 00:22:10.061
The edges are really sharp.

00:22:10.128 --> 00:22:13.865
All in all, I think this is
a really well-crafted sword.

00:22:13.965 --> 00:22:15.299
Held up very nicely--

00:22:15.366 --> 00:22:17.336
there's just no
damage on this edge.

00:22:23.709 --> 00:22:27.079
[striking sound]

00:22:44.363 --> 00:22:48.166
All right, right off,
this thing's a destroyer.

00:22:48.266 --> 00:22:49.668
[laughter]

00:22:49.734 --> 00:22:54.005
It's not outside the
realm of proper weight.

00:22:54.106 --> 00:22:56.208
This is kind of
the outside edge.

00:22:56.274 --> 00:22:59.344
When cutting, you feel
the blade slow down,

00:22:59.444 --> 00:23:02.213
as opposed to just pass
through the tatami mat,

00:23:02.279 --> 00:23:03.748
so it's got a lot of drag on it.

00:23:03.848 --> 00:23:05.816
And that really has to do with
the thickness of the blade

00:23:05.883 --> 00:23:08.319
and the style of the
grind that's on this edge.

00:23:08.386 --> 00:23:10.622
But it held up
well and cut good.

00:23:10.689 --> 00:23:11.723
Good job.

00:23:16.328 --> 00:23:17.729
GRADY POWELL: All right,
bladesmiths, the time

00:23:17.829 --> 00:23:19.397
has come to find
out if, Ben, you're

00:23:19.464 --> 00:23:21.165
going to keep your
unbeaten streak going

00:23:21.265 --> 00:23:22.900
or if, Rob, you've
dethroned the king

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:24.702
and you're taking home the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:23:24.803 --> 00:23:26.871
champion and a
check for $10,000.

00:23:26.938 --> 00:23:28.740
I got to say, this
was a very close race,

00:23:28.840 --> 00:23:30.809
and you made a difficult
decision for the judges.

00:23:30.909 --> 00:23:33.077
Today's "Forged in
Fire" champion is--

00:23:33.178 --> 00:23:36.681
[music playing]

00:23:39.451 --> 00:23:41.019
--Ben Abbott.

00:23:41.119 --> 00:23:42.254
Ben, congratulations.

00:23:42.354 --> 00:23:43.788
You are now 6 and 0.

00:23:43.888 --> 00:23:46.457
Now, Rob, you gave him an
unbelievable run for his money.

00:23:46.558 --> 00:23:48.560
But unfortunately, your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:23:48.660 --> 00:23:50.161
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:23:50.228 --> 00:23:51.596
step off the forge floor.
- All right, well, thank you.

00:23:51.662 --> 00:23:52.864
I had a great time.
HOST: Thank you so much.

00:23:52.931 --> 00:23:54.198
HOST: Hey, Rob, nice
job on that blade.

00:23:54.265 --> 00:23:55.333
Thank you.

00:23:55.433 --> 00:23:56.701
I'm going to go
home, see my family,

00:23:56.768 --> 00:24:00.672
and make a really nice
Irish ring-hilted sword.

00:24:00.738 --> 00:24:05.277
And it's going to take me a
lot longer than just 9 hours.

00:24:05.377 --> 00:24:08.279
GRADY POWELL: Well, Ben,
that's 6 and 0, buddy.

00:24:08.346 --> 00:24:09.613
You are unbelievable.

00:24:09.714 --> 00:24:11.716
You are, yet again, the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:24:11.817 --> 00:24:13.318
Congratulations.

00:24:13.385 --> 00:24:14.319
I can't believe it.

00:24:14.386 --> 00:24:15.853
I can't believe it.

00:24:15.953 --> 00:24:19.824
Rob is a great smith, a really
fun guy, a great competitor,

00:24:19.924 --> 00:24:21.960
and I'm really happy to
have worked next to him.

00:24:22.026 --> 00:24:23.428
GRADY POWELL: It looks
like you're keeping

00:24:23.495 --> 00:24:24.896
the unbeaten streak alive.

00:24:24.963 --> 00:24:26.264
Congratulations, man.

00:24:26.331 --> 00:24:27.465
You're not done yet.

00:24:27.565 --> 00:24:29.134
We got more to go.
I hope you're ready.

00:24:29.234 --> 00:24:30.267
Oh, my god.
What did I sign up for?

00:24:30.368 --> 00:24:31.369
Good job, bud.

00:24:31.436 --> 00:24:33.605
[clapping]

00:24:35.039 --> 00:24:38.877
For those that are coming to
try to beat me, I'm still here.

00:24:38.977 --> 00:24:40.010
I'm still undefeated.

00:24:40.077 --> 00:24:41.079
Bring it on.

00:24:44.082 --> 00:24:45.149
HOST: The Chinese war sword.

00:24:45.216 --> 00:24:46.251
Oh.

00:24:48.953 --> 00:24:50.654
NARRATOR: The 17th
century Chinese war sword

00:24:50.755 --> 00:24:53.925
was used in battle starting
in the Qing dynasty

00:24:53.992 --> 00:24:55.393
through 20th century.

00:24:55.460 --> 00:24:57.896
Primarily used by peasant
armies, this large,

00:24:57.963 --> 00:24:59.697
two handed-weapon
fatally slashed

00:24:59.764 --> 00:25:03.034
and chopped through more
than 3,000 Japanese forces

00:25:03.101 --> 00:25:04.603
during World War II.

00:25:04.669 --> 00:25:06.905
This deadly blade previously
appeared on season 7 of "Forged

00:25:07.005 --> 00:25:09.741
in Fire," where both smiths
struggled with the weight

00:25:09.807 --> 00:25:11.709
and size of this massive sword.

00:25:11.809 --> 00:25:14.412
But in the end, one
smith's weapon fell victim

00:25:14.479 --> 00:25:17.815
to the dreaded ice block.

00:25:17.882 --> 00:25:19.384
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, bladesmiths--

00:25:19.484 --> 00:25:20.985
two beautiful swords.

00:25:21.052 --> 00:25:24.089
But now, it's time to find
out how lethal they are.

00:25:24.155 --> 00:25:27.191
This is the dynamic kill test.

00:25:27.292 --> 00:25:28.293
Shall we begin?

00:25:31.029 --> 00:25:35.000
[chopping sound]

00:25:55.386 --> 00:25:56.555
Holy cow.

00:26:02.660 --> 00:26:03.928
All right, gents.

00:26:03.995 --> 00:26:06.697
On this blue anvil weapon,
when you pick it up,

00:26:06.797 --> 00:26:08.232
it's got that forward weight.

00:26:08.332 --> 00:26:11.135
But being a two-handed sword,
it actually is comfortable.

00:26:11.202 --> 00:26:14.672
Now, in terms of the edge,
well, pretty much demolished

00:26:14.739 --> 00:26:16.007
this ballistics dummy.

00:26:16.074 --> 00:26:18.643
Overall, it will kill.

00:26:22.746 --> 00:26:25.116
Caleb's blade played
performed really well.

00:26:25.183 --> 00:26:28.486
If my blade takes a bend
when Caleb's did not,

00:26:28.552 --> 00:26:32.023
it's over for me.

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:35.694
[chopping sound]

00:27:03.221 --> 00:27:04.889
DOUG MARCAIDA: All right,
guys, right off the bat,

00:27:04.989 --> 00:27:08.059
it is a light weapon to wield.

00:27:08.126 --> 00:27:09.494
The edge is very sharp.

00:27:09.560 --> 00:27:11.796
And in every cut,
it was very deep.

00:27:11.896 --> 00:27:14.733
Overall, this
weapon-- it will kill.

00:27:21.739 --> 00:27:23.240
DAVID BAKER: All right,
gentlemen, it's time

00:27:23.340 --> 00:27:24.775
for the dynamic strength test.

00:27:24.842 --> 00:27:28.612
We've got bamboo and cane in
our bamboo forest over here.

00:27:28.679 --> 00:27:30.348
Blue weapon is up first.

00:27:30.415 --> 00:27:31.448
You both ready?

00:27:31.515 --> 00:27:33.017
Let's do it.

00:27:33.084 --> 00:27:36.655
[music playing]

00:27:39.024 --> 00:27:42.661
[chopping sound]

00:28:19.698 --> 00:28:21.399
DAVID BAKER: All right,
so the blue anvil sword--

00:28:21.466 --> 00:28:25.136
it's a heavy piece, and
it's very forward-weighted.

00:28:25.236 --> 00:28:26.070
Edge held up nice.

00:28:26.137 --> 00:28:27.671
When I run my finger
down it, there's

00:28:27.738 --> 00:28:29.374
one spot that I
can feel something,

00:28:29.474 --> 00:28:32.343
but literally have to run
my fingernail down that edge

00:28:32.443 --> 00:28:33.444
to feel it.

00:28:33.544 --> 00:28:35.512
All in all, held up beautifully.

00:28:35.613 --> 00:28:38.382
Can't complain.

00:28:38.483 --> 00:28:41.486
[music playing]

00:28:44.823 --> 00:28:48.393
[chopping sound]

00:29:26.931 --> 00:29:31.202
All right, as far as the edge
goes, no damage whatsoever.

00:29:31.302 --> 00:29:33.070
The decorative touches
are nice, but what

00:29:33.137 --> 00:29:36.473
I really like about this
blade is its functionality.

00:29:36.540 --> 00:29:37.508
All-around, good blade.

00:29:37.575 --> 00:29:38.777
Really nicely done.

00:29:45.249 --> 00:29:46.450
GRADY POWELL:
Bladesmiths, this has

00:29:46.517 --> 00:29:48.152
been an awesome competition.

00:29:48.252 --> 00:29:51.155
But the time has come for us
to find out if, Ben, you're

00:29:51.222 --> 00:29:52.991
going to remain undefeated
or if, Caleb, you're

00:29:53.091 --> 00:29:55.126
going to be first one
to take down the champ

00:29:55.226 --> 00:29:56.794
and go home with the
title of "Forged in Fire"

00:29:56.860 --> 00:29:59.964
champion and get a
check for $10,000.

00:30:00.064 --> 00:30:02.666
Our judges had quite
the discussion,

00:30:02.733 --> 00:30:05.436
but they came up with
a common decision.

00:30:05.536 --> 00:30:08.205
The winner of today's "Forged
in Fire" competition is--

00:30:08.306 --> 00:30:11.075
[music playing]

00:30:12.443 --> 00:30:13.377
--Ben Abbott.

00:30:13.444 --> 00:30:14.344
You have done it again.

00:30:14.445 --> 00:30:16.080
Congratulations.

00:30:16.146 --> 00:30:18.849
Caleb, you built a beautiful,
strong, and sharp blade.

00:30:18.950 --> 00:30:20.985
But unfortunately, it
didn't make the cut today.

00:30:21.085 --> 00:30:22.553
And Dave Baker is
going to tell you why.

00:30:22.620 --> 00:30:23.755
DAVID BAKER: Ben's
blade with that

00:30:23.855 --> 00:30:25.790
dragon and pattern
and the handle wrap

00:30:25.857 --> 00:30:27.658
was just more impressive.

00:30:27.758 --> 00:30:29.027
Absolutely.

00:30:29.127 --> 00:30:31.028
Now, Caleb, it's been an
honor watching you work.

00:30:31.095 --> 00:30:32.597
But unfortunately,
at this point,

00:30:32.664 --> 00:30:33.731
I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:30:33.798 --> 00:30:35.500
step off the forge floor.

00:30:35.567 --> 00:30:36.667
- Thank you, Ben.
- Good fight.

00:30:36.734 --> 00:30:37.835
- That was awesome.
- Good fight.

00:30:37.902 --> 00:30:39.203
- Thank you so much.
- Good job.

00:30:39.304 --> 00:30:40.304
CALEB LEDFORD: Thank you all.
- Good job, Caleb.

00:30:40.371 --> 00:30:41.506
Ben, that's it, man.

00:30:41.573 --> 00:30:43.540
You are now 7 and
0 in this forge.

00:30:43.607 --> 00:30:44.675
Congratulations, buddy.

00:30:44.775 --> 00:30:45.743
Jeez Louise.

00:30:45.810 --> 00:30:47.011
[applause]

00:30:47.077 --> 00:30:50.114
Oh, my god, I just won
another competition.

00:30:50.215 --> 00:30:51.816
I'm now 7 and 0.

00:30:51.916 --> 00:30:53.184
This is phenomenal.

00:30:53.251 --> 00:30:54.952
I'm almost kind
of starting to get

00:30:55.018 --> 00:30:57.254
used to the winning this thing.

00:30:57.321 --> 00:30:59.557
Among all your blades
that I've ever wielded,

00:30:59.623 --> 00:31:01.359
I'd say this is the best one.

00:31:01.425 --> 00:31:02.927
Thank you so much.

00:31:02.994 --> 00:31:04.962
The only issue, now, of course,
is that every time I win,

00:31:05.062 --> 00:31:07.365
I'm more, and more, and
more afraid of a loss.

00:31:10.401 --> 00:31:11.469
HOST: The Ida sword.

00:31:11.569 --> 00:31:15.205
[laughs] Oh, the Ida.

00:31:15.272 --> 00:31:17.876
NARRATOR: The Ida sword used
by the Yoruba people of West

00:31:17.942 --> 00:31:20.978
Africa features a double-edge,
leaf-shaped blade ideal

00:31:21.045 --> 00:31:22.947
for harvesting
crops in the fields,

00:31:23.014 --> 00:31:26.250
as well as inflicting lethal
slashes and stabs in battle.

00:31:26.350 --> 00:31:29.888
This deadly weapon appeared in
season 4 of "Forged in Fire,"

00:31:29.954 --> 00:31:32.790
where both smiths produced
ornate, Damascus patterns,

00:31:32.890 --> 00:31:35.058
but one smith's mistake
during his quench

00:31:35.159 --> 00:31:37.428
caused the sword to chip
during the strength test,

00:31:37.495 --> 00:31:40.731
costing him the competition.

00:31:40.798 --> 00:31:42.466
Your time starts now.

00:31:42.533 --> 00:31:46.804
5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:31:46.904 --> 00:31:48.439
Great work.

00:31:48.506 --> 00:31:50.808
Please put down your blades and
prepare yourselves for testing.

00:31:50.875 --> 00:31:52.042
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, bladesmiths,

00:31:52.142 --> 00:31:55.112
welcome to dynamic kill test.

00:31:55.212 --> 00:31:57.047
To find out how lethal
your Ida swords are,

00:31:57.114 --> 00:31:58.649
I'm going to cut through
this ballistics dummy

00:31:58.716 --> 00:32:00.351
and pork loins.
You guys ready?

00:32:00.451 --> 00:32:01.386
Let's do it.

00:32:01.452 --> 00:32:03.688
CONTESTANT: All
right, let's do this.

00:32:03.755 --> 00:32:07.591
[music playing]

00:32:07.692 --> 00:32:11.329
[chopping sound]

00:32:31.049 --> 00:32:32.983
All right, guys, the first
thing about this is when you

00:32:33.083 --> 00:32:34.952
pick it up, it's
forward-heavy because you

00:32:35.052 --> 00:32:37.855
have thicker grinds right here.

00:32:37.922 --> 00:32:40.458
But when you swing
it, it's manageable.

00:32:40.558 --> 00:32:43.093
I like the flare that you put
over there because it's really

00:32:43.160 --> 00:32:45.863
giving me a nice
counterbalance, especially

00:32:45.963 --> 00:32:46.997
when you're swinging
something that

00:32:47.097 --> 00:32:48.932
has a forward weight to it.

00:32:48.999 --> 00:32:52.070
Overall, it will kill.

00:32:54.739 --> 00:32:57.976
[music playing]

00:33:01.346 --> 00:33:04.749
[chopping sound]

00:33:25.403 --> 00:33:28.338
All right, gentlemen,
when I pick up this blade,

00:33:28.405 --> 00:33:31.241
I can feel the
distribution of the weight

00:33:31.308 --> 00:33:34.479
be far more even compared
to gold's over here.

00:33:34.545 --> 00:33:37.481
When I'm cutting this,
because of that distribution,

00:33:37.581 --> 00:33:41.219
it's even a deeper chop
into this ballistics dummy.

00:33:41.319 --> 00:33:44.121
Now, when I'm grabbing
on to the handle here,

00:33:44.188 --> 00:33:45.522
actually, it feels good.

00:33:45.622 --> 00:33:48.159
It's so forward, I can really
tell where the edge is.

00:33:48.259 --> 00:33:50.795
Overall, it will kill.

00:33:53.865 --> 00:33:56.434
[music playing]

00:33:56.501 --> 00:33:58.168
DAVID BAKER: All
right, gentlemen,

00:33:58.235 --> 00:33:59.604
it's time for our combined
strength and sharpness test--

00:33:59.670 --> 00:34:03.573
the ammo crate chop
and foam dummy slice.

00:34:03.674 --> 00:34:04.975
Gold anvil's up.

00:34:05.076 --> 00:34:08.946
[music playing]

00:34:09.013 --> 00:34:12.583
[chopping sound]

00:34:26.964 --> 00:34:29.333
So right off, when you
pick up this weapon,

00:34:29.400 --> 00:34:31.702
there's a lot of weight
up here in this blade.

00:34:31.769 --> 00:34:36.174
But in that test, the blade
took a warp right there.

00:34:36.240 --> 00:34:40.011
As far as the edges of the blade
go, they held up quite well.

00:34:40.078 --> 00:34:44.881
But there's really no
getting around that bend.

00:34:44.982 --> 00:34:48.486
[music playing]

00:34:51.856 --> 00:34:54.826
[chopping sound]

00:35:14.412 --> 00:35:17.248
All right, this thing
is a superior cutter.

00:35:17.314 --> 00:35:19.350
Those cuts took
maybe half the effort

00:35:19.416 --> 00:35:22.152
to get deeper into that target.

00:35:22.219 --> 00:35:25.789
As far as the strength test
goes, it took no damage.

00:35:25.856 --> 00:35:27.125
Nice piece.

00:35:31.628 --> 00:35:33.230
GRADY POWELL: Well,
bladesmiths, in 8 hours,

00:35:33.297 --> 00:35:34.832
you were both tasked
to build a very

00:35:34.899 --> 00:35:37.635
difficult blade with an even
more difficult technique.

00:35:37.735 --> 00:35:40.604
But in this competition, only
one of you can come out on top.

00:35:40.671 --> 00:35:43.574
The winner of today's "Forged
in Fire" competition is--

00:35:43.641 --> 00:35:46.277
[music playing]

00:35:49.146 --> 00:35:50.080
Ben Abbott.

00:35:50.147 --> 00:35:51.849
You are now 8 and 0, buddy.

00:35:51.916 --> 00:35:53.250
Congratulations.

00:35:53.316 --> 00:35:55.052
Brent, I'm going to have
to ask you to please

00:35:55.119 --> 00:35:57.855
step off the forge floor.

00:35:57.922 --> 00:35:59.990
I was able to do something
pretty incredible, I think,

00:36:00.057 --> 00:36:01.225
in 8.

00:36:01.291 --> 00:36:02.759
Hours but Ben's a
whole other level.

00:36:02.859 --> 00:36:05.663
It looks like he took 4 days
on it like a normal challenge.

00:36:05.730 --> 00:36:06.697
Unbelievable.

00:36:06.797 --> 00:36:07.832
I'm a two-time loser.

00:36:13.271 --> 00:36:15.406
Ben, Ben, Ben.

00:36:15.472 --> 00:36:18.009
A current record of
8 and 0 in the forge.

00:36:18.109 --> 00:36:19.009
How are you feeling?

00:36:19.076 --> 00:36:20.010
I feel amazing.

00:36:20.110 --> 00:36:22.947
I'm super excited.

00:36:23.013 --> 00:36:24.382
Brent is such an amazing smith.

00:36:24.482 --> 00:36:28.352
And to be able to pull
off a win against him--

00:36:28.418 --> 00:36:30.421
I just feel absolutely amazing.

00:36:30.487 --> 00:36:32.690
But here I am, still undefeated.

00:36:32.790 --> 00:36:35.959
With any luck, I'll be able to
keep the streak alive for ever

00:36:36.026 --> 00:36:36.961
and a day.

00:36:37.061 --> 00:36:38.028
There's a lot of
smiths out there

00:36:38.094 --> 00:36:39.463
that might want to take me down.

00:36:39.564 --> 00:36:40.631
But I'm here.

00:36:40.698 --> 00:36:41.598
I'm ready.

00:36:41.665 --> 00:36:42.733
Bring it on.

00:36:46.637 --> 00:36:48.706
HOST: The spatha.

00:36:48.772 --> 00:36:52.443
NARRATOR: The spatha sword dates
back to third century Rome.

00:36:52.509 --> 00:36:55.412
This cavalry weapon features
a straight, double-edged blade

00:36:55.479 --> 00:36:58.215
that allows for deeper,
deadlier cuts and thrusts

00:36:58.281 --> 00:37:00.283
than the shorter
gladius sword previously

00:37:00.350 --> 00:37:02.086
used by the Roman soldiers.

00:37:02.153 --> 00:37:04.722
First featured in season
7 of "Forged in Fire,"

00:37:04.822 --> 00:37:07.525
two smiths impressed the judges
with their ornate versions

00:37:07.592 --> 00:37:08.859
of this blade.

00:37:08.959 --> 00:37:11.262
However, one smith's failure to
include one of the parameters--

00:37:11.329 --> 00:37:12.229
a medial ridge--

00:37:12.329 --> 00:37:14.798
cost him the competition.

00:37:14.865 --> 00:37:16.900
DOUG MARCAIDA: Bladesmiths
welcome to the dynamic kill

00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:18.202
test.

00:37:18.268 --> 00:37:19.837
I'm going to deliver
some slashes and thrusts

00:37:19.904 --> 00:37:22.773
on this pig carcass and try to
cut through these tatami mats.

00:37:22.840 --> 00:37:24.308
The blue anvil is up first.

00:37:28.279 --> 00:37:31.482
[chopping sound]

00:38:01.845 --> 00:38:03.947
All right, gentlemen, first
up, when you're looking at this

00:38:04.014 --> 00:38:07.317
handle here, because it's a
forward-weight on the sword,

00:38:07.384 --> 00:38:09.419
there's no counterbalance
here that--

00:38:09.519 --> 00:38:11.488
every time I'm swinging this--

00:38:11.555 --> 00:38:13.924
the blade wants
to leave my hand.

00:38:14.025 --> 00:38:19.429
But these cuts onto the
pig carcass are very deep.

00:38:19.496 --> 00:38:22.533
But overall, this
weapon, it will kill.

00:38:22.633 --> 00:38:24.301
The bar has been
set really high.

00:38:24.401 --> 00:38:26.070
I just hope mine can match it.

00:38:29.407 --> 00:38:32.576
[chopping sound]

00:38:33.944 --> 00:38:36.981
[music playing]

00:39:06.476 --> 00:39:07.911
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, gentlemen,

00:39:07.978 --> 00:39:11.181
so the balance of the blade
is back toward the handle,

00:39:11.248 --> 00:39:13.250
so it's easier to control.

00:39:13.317 --> 00:39:15.452
The edges took no damage.

00:39:15.518 --> 00:39:18.488
On the pig carcass,
the weight distribution

00:39:18.555 --> 00:39:21.124
of slashing with this
actually cuts very deep.

00:39:21.224 --> 00:39:24.428
Overall, this
weapon, it will kill.

00:39:29.367 --> 00:39:31.268
All right, gentlemen,
it's time for our dynamic

00:39:31.368 --> 00:39:32.936
strength and sharpness
test-- the clay

00:39:33.003 --> 00:39:35.439
pot smash and fish slice.

00:39:35.506 --> 00:39:38.042
This is all about the edge
retention of your blade,

00:39:38.108 --> 00:39:40.711
how well they cut, and how
well they feel in my hand.

00:39:40.778 --> 00:39:43.747
So gentlemen, it's
time to start.

00:39:43.814 --> 00:39:45.048
[music playing]

00:39:45.149 --> 00:39:47.785
[chopping sound]

00:40:10.674 --> 00:40:12.809
All right, so it held
its edge, which is great.

00:40:12.876 --> 00:40:16.614
The weight's not an issue other
than, once you finish a swing,

00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:18.115
the recovery is a
little bit slower.

00:40:18.215 --> 00:40:19.182
But it held up well.

00:40:19.249 --> 00:40:20.418
Good job.

00:40:31.796 --> 00:40:35.065
[chopping sound]

00:40:35.132 --> 00:40:38.102
[music playing]

00:40:58.222 --> 00:40:59.690
All right, so, right
off, when I pick

00:40:59.790 --> 00:41:01.625
up the sword, what I feel more
than anything is the balance.

00:41:01.725 --> 00:41:03.961
You want that balance
point right there.

00:41:04.028 --> 00:41:05.462
The pattern is beautiful.

00:41:05.529 --> 00:41:07.865
The edge held up really
well and cut well.

00:41:07.931 --> 00:41:10.968
And though I love the attempt
at historical accuracy

00:41:11.068 --> 00:41:14.270
in this handle, it would have
been nice to see a little bit

00:41:14.337 --> 00:41:16.040
more finish work done on it.

00:41:16.106 --> 00:41:18.308
Having said that, when
I put it in my hand,

00:41:18.375 --> 00:41:19.844
it fits really nicely.

00:41:19.910 --> 00:41:20.945
It's nicely done.

00:41:25.782 --> 00:41:27.250
GRADY POWELL: Well,
bladesmiths, it comes

00:41:27.317 --> 00:41:29.186
down to this final moment.

00:41:29.252 --> 00:41:30.554
You both did a phenomenal job.

00:41:30.654 --> 00:41:33.090
Judges agree, both your
blades tested almost evenly,

00:41:33.190 --> 00:41:36.093
so it came down to the
very finest of details.

00:41:36.193 --> 00:41:37.694
The stakes are really high.

00:41:37.761 --> 00:41:39.930
Ben, if you win, you will remain
undefeated and go to a record

00:41:39.997 --> 00:41:41.798
of 9 wins and 0 losses.

00:41:41.865 --> 00:41:44.134
Our judges discussed
your blade, and they came

00:41:44.234 --> 00:41:45.669
out with a final conclusion.

00:41:45.736 --> 00:41:48.005
And the winner of today's
"Forged in Fire" competition

00:41:48.105 --> 00:41:49.006
is--

00:41:49.073 --> 00:41:51.709
[music playing]

00:41:53.010 --> 00:41:54.545
--he has done it again--

00:41:54.611 --> 00:41:56.179
Ben Abbott.
Congratulations.

00:41:56.246 --> 00:41:57.314
Oh, my god.
Oh, my god.

00:41:57.381 --> 00:41:58.815
- Congratulations.
- Oh, my god.

00:41:58.915 --> 00:42:00.383
Nicholas,
unfortunately, your blade

00:42:00.483 --> 00:42:02.019
didn't come out on top today.

00:42:02.119 --> 00:42:03.119
You smoked the competition.

00:42:03.219 --> 00:42:04.521
You did a phenomenal job here.

00:42:04.587 --> 00:42:05.789
But unfortunately,
at this time, I'm

00:42:05.856 --> 00:42:06.757
going to have to
ask you to please

00:42:06.824 --> 00:42:08.125
step off the forge floor.

00:42:08.192 --> 00:42:09.493
- Thank you guys very much.
- Thank you so much.

00:42:09.593 --> 00:42:11.395
- See you, Nick.
- Nice job, man.

00:42:11.462 --> 00:42:12.462
NICHOLAS COCHIOLO:
I did my best.

00:42:12.529 --> 00:42:13.630
Ben came out on top.

00:42:13.697 --> 00:42:15.098
Totally deserves the win.

00:42:15.165 --> 00:42:17.333
Ben Abbott, we are running
out of fingers to count on.

00:42:17.400 --> 00:42:19.235
You are the champion, again.

00:42:19.302 --> 00:42:20.236
9 and 0.

00:42:20.303 --> 00:42:21.204
Buddy, how do you feel?

00:42:21.305 --> 00:42:22.573
I feel amazing.

00:42:22.639 --> 00:42:24.507
So much of me has gone
into it blood-wise,

00:42:24.574 --> 00:42:27.544
but I'm just super jealous
that they paid off.

00:42:27.611 --> 00:42:31.181
I just became a "Forged
in Fire" champion again.

00:42:31.247 --> 00:42:32.749
I am just elated.

00:42:32.816 --> 00:42:35.219
This is probably one of the
best experiences of my life

00:42:35.285 --> 00:42:38.054
to go through five competitions
and win all five of them

00:42:38.121 --> 00:42:38.956
in a row.

00:42:39.023 --> 00:42:40.424
DOUG MARCAIDA: The
blade, I'd say,

00:42:40.490 --> 00:42:42.292
right now, that's
the most stunning

00:42:42.392 --> 00:42:43.593
pattern that you've presented.

00:42:43.693 --> 00:42:45.228
In each of these
competitions, I've learned

00:42:45.295 --> 00:42:46.363
a little bit of somethings.

00:42:46.430 --> 00:42:47.497
You have to learn
how to be fast.

00:42:47.564 --> 00:42:48.632
You have to learn
how to be good.

00:42:48.699 --> 00:42:50.200
You have to learn
how to be smart.

00:42:50.266 --> 00:42:52.235
And I just feel like my skill
is getting better and better

00:42:52.335 --> 00:42:53.270
as I go.

00:42:53.337 --> 00:42:55.439
Where do you go from here?

00:42:55.539 --> 00:42:57.106
Dave, you ready to compete?

00:42:57.173 --> 00:42:58.141
Sign me up.

00:42:58.208 --> 00:42:59.643
Oh, hell yes.

00:42:59.743 --> 00:43:01.211
I'm currently 9 and 0.

00:43:01.278 --> 00:43:02.646
I'm unbeaten.

00:43:02.713 --> 00:43:04.881
If you think you got what
it takes, bring it on.

00:43:04.948 --> 00:43:06.350
I'm ready.

